# Recipe Finder Agent Workflow

Build with specialized agents — do not implement the entire assignment in one shot.

## Required preamble (every agent)

At the start of every agent task:

> Read ARCHITECTURE.md and inspect the existing implementation before making changes. Do not rewrite working functionality. Preserve existing conventions and integrate with the existing architecture.

## Run order

1. `architecture` → ARCHITECTURE.md only (no features)
2. `stencil-component-library` → packages/recipe-ui
3. `api-data-layer` → apps/web data/API layer
4. `sveltekit-ui` → app shell + routes
5. Then in parallel if needed: `recipe-management`, `favorites`, `meal-planner`
6. `stencil-svelte-integration` → INTEGRATION.md
7. `testing-quality` → tests + fixes
8. `deployment-npm` → RELEASE.md + README (no invented URLs)
9. `final-review` → ASSIGNMENT_REVIEW.md

## Hard constraints

- Stack: Svelte 5 + SvelteKit + TypeScript + StencilJS
- SvelteKit consumes the **published** Stencil npm package — never Stencil source
- Demonstrate props, custom events, and slots
- Prefer simple production architecture over unnecessary complexity
